    storyText: 'Study Planner Pro exists because most students spend more time organizing their study materials than actually studying. The semester starts, and suddenly there are six subjects, twenty deadlines, and no single view of everything.',
    storyText2: 'This planner is that single view. Enter your subjects and dates once. It generates a complete semester system — weekly spreads that reflect your schedule, a revision tracker that monitors topic coverage, an exam countdown that keeps deadlines visible. You stop organizing and start studying.',
    whoFor: 'For the student who wants every subject, deadline, and exam visible — not scattered across five notebooks and a calendar app.'
  },
  "master-your-day": {
    features: [
      { icon: '🔄', title: 'Weekly Reset', description: 'A 7-step Sunday ritual that closes the past week and sets up the next one. Wins, challenges, priorities — done in 15 minutes.' },
      { icon: '⚡', title: 'Daily Command Center', description: 'Your energy, mood, Big 3 priorities, and an hourly schedule that respects your rhythm — morning peak, afternoon slump, evening wind-down.' },
      { icon: '🌙', title: 'Evening Reflection', description: 'Close your day with clarity. What went well, what distracted you, how you feel — and a plan for better sleep.' },
      { icon: '🧠', title: 'Priority Engine', description: 'Score tasks by impact, urgency, and energy fit. Know what to work on now and what can wait.' },
      { icon: '🧩', title: 'Anti-Procrastination Dashboard', description: 'Overwhelming tasks split into micro-actions. Time estimates, reason tags, worst-case analysis. Commit and start moving.' },
      { icon: '🌿', title: 'Energy & Mood Tracker', description: 'AM and PM check-ins that reveal your patterns. See what drains you, what fuels you, and when you do your best work.' },
      { icon: '⏱️', title: 'Time Audit', description: 'Log your day in hourly blocks. Compare how you thought you spent it with how it actually went.' },
      { icon: '🧹', title: 'Brain Dump Processor', description: 'Empty your mind onto the page. Categorize into Tasks, Ideas, Worries, and Later — nothing gets lost.' },
      { icon: '🔥', title: 'Habit Streak Analytics', description: 'Track 8 habits on a 28-day continuous grid. See your streaks, your gaps, and your growth.' }
    ],
    faqs: [
      { q: 'How is this different from a daily planner?', a: 'A daily planner shows you today. Master Your Day is a system that connects your weekly reset to your daily command to your evening reflection. Every page feeds the next, so nothing lives in isolation.' },
      { q: 'How much time does it take each day?', a: 'Morning check-in: 2-3 minutes. Evening reflection: 2-3 minutes. Weekly Reset: 10-15 minutes on Sunday. Designed to be sustainable, not overwhelming.' },
      { q: 'What pages are included?', a: '11 connected pages: Cover, Dashboard, Weekly Reset (7-step ritual), Daily Command Center (hourly schedule), Evening Reflection, Priority Engine, Anti-Procrastination Dashboard, Energy & Mood Tracker (AM/PM), Time Audit, Brain Dump Processor, and Habit Streak Analytics (8 habits).' },
      { q: 'What makes it interactive?', a: 'Energy sliders, mood selectors, star ratings, habit grid cells, commit buttons — all save automatically. It feels like a living system, not a static document.' },
      { q: 'Is there a live web app?', a: 'Yes. After purchase you get access to the full interactive app at /app/master-your-day. Open your browser and start planning. Works on any device.' }
    ],
    storyTitle: 'For anyone who wants to stop managing tasks and start doing meaningful work.',
    storyText: 'Most productivity systems are designed by people who have never struggled with procrastination. They assume you already know what matters and just need a place to write it down.',
    storyText2: 'Master Your Day was built differently. It assumes you have competing priorities, fluctuating energy, and a brain that sometimes refuses to start. So it gives you a Sunday ritual to set direction, a daily command center that adapts to your energy, and an evening reflection that captures progress without judgment. Not a system for perfect people. A system for real humans.',
